        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Drain Life"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(divine, necromancy)\n\nWhen the wight damages a living creature with its claw Strike, the wight gains 3 temporary Hit Points and the creature must succeed at a DC 17 Fortitude save or become drained 1. Further damage dealt by the wraith increases the amount of drain by 1 on a failed save to a maximum of drained 4."
            },
            "id": "d1ba39d2-c8cc-40d4-a9de-a29108577621",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-17T12:41:25.944969"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Wight Spawn"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(divine, necromancy)\n\nA living humanoid slain by a wight's claw Strike rises as a wight after 1d4 rounds. This wight spawn is under the command of the wight that killed it. It doesn't have Drain Life or Wight Spawn and becomes clumsy 2 for as long as it is a wight spawn. If the creator of the wight spawn dies, the wight spawn becomes a full-fledged, autonomous wight; it regains its free will, gains Drain Life and Wight Spawn, and is no longer clumsy."
            },
            "id": "a4cb3eb1-d01b-4a91-ab21-d406ef4de349",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-17T12:41:25.944969"
            }
          }
        }
